# AstroWay API, for code in this project

Standalone rule: copy to `.cursor/rules/astroway.mdc` in a project that does not use the AstroWay plugin. Full playbook: https://api.astroway.info/AGENTS.md. Index for models: https://api.astroway.info/llms.txt.

## Never guess

- Never invent a path, field, enum value or tool name. Look it up with `find_endpoint` on the keyless MCP server `https://mcp.astroway.info/mcp/docs`, or in `https://api.astroway.info/v1/openapi.json` (paths are relative to `/v1`). If it is not there, the API does not have it.
- Ask the user for birth date, time and place. Never default a time to noon.

## Request contract

- Base URL `https://api.astroway.info/v1`. Header `X-Api-Key: <key>` read from `process.env.ASTROWAY_API_KEY` (or the language's equivalent). JSON body on POST.
- Coordinates: `latitude`, `longitude` in decimal degrees. `lat`, `lng`, `lon`, `tz` are `400 INVALID_FIELD`. The API does not geocode; resolve the place first.
- Time zone: `timezone` as an IANA name (`Europe/Kyiv`) or `"auto"`; the server resolves the offset for that date. `timezoneOffset` (hours, `5.5`) only when the offset is known. **Neither means UTC, silently.**
- `date` `YYYY-MM-DD`; `time` `HH:mm` or `HH:mm:ss`, local. Unknown time: `timeUnknown: true` on `/v1/chart` and `/v1/synastry` only.
- Two people: `chart1` and `chart2`, each a full birth object.
- Smaller answers: `?fields=planets.name,planets.longitude,houses.ascendant&precision=2`.

## Responses and errors

- `{ "ok": true, "data": ... }` or `{ "ok": false, "error": { "code", "message", "details"?, "docs"? } }`. Branch on `error.code`; show `error.message` to the user.
- Retry network errors and `5xx` with backoff, `429 RATE_LIMIT` after `Retry-After`. Do not retry other `4xx`, and never `CREDITS_EXHAUSTED`, `SPEND_CAP_REACHED` or `PLAN_UPGRADE_REQUIRED`.
- Error reference: https://api.astroway.info/en/errors/.

## Keys, cost and limits

- The key is a server secret. An ordinary key answers `403 ORIGIN_FORBIDDEN` to any request with an `Origin` or `Referer`, so call it from a server route or API handler. Never expose it under `NEXT_PUBLIC_`, `VITE_` or in client bundles. Browser use needs a publishable `pk_` key bound to the site's domains.
- `aw_test_` keys are sandbox: same paths, no credits, but AI interpretation, reports and rendering answer `402 SANDBOX_ENDPOINT_UNAVAILABLE`.
- Prices: natal chart 20 credits, planets or moon phase 10, sign horoscope 50, interpretation 100, PDF reports thousands. Every response reports `X-Credits-Used` and `X-Credits-Remaining`. Price list: https://api.astroway.info/en/credits/.
- An identical request within 5 minutes is a cache hit at 0 credits. Still store charts: a natal chart for a fixed birth never changes.
- Put a rate limit in front of any public page that spends the key. Keyed limits are per minute by plan and reported in `X-RateLimit-*`.

## Common endpoints

| Need | Endpoint |
|---|---|
| Natal chart | `POST /v1/chart` |
| Sign horoscope (no birth data) | `POST /v1/horoscope/daily`, `/weekly`, `/monthly`, `/yearly` |
| Compatibility | `POST /v1/synastry`, `POST /v1/match/score` |
| Transits | `POST /v1/transits`, `POST /v1/transit-calendar` |
| Vedic | `POST /v1/vedic/kundli`, `POST /v1/vedic/panchang/full` |
| BaZi | `POST /v1/bazi/chart` |
| Human Design | `POST /v1/human-design` |
| Tarot | `POST /v1/tarot/rider-waite/draw/three-card` |
| Chart image | `POST /v1/render/wheel-western` |

Everything else: https://api.astroway.info/llms-full.txt lists every operation with its price and required fields.

## SDKs

`npm install @astroway/sdk`, `pip install astroway`, `composer require astroway/sdk`, `go get github.com/astroway/astroway-go`, `dotnet add package Astroway.Sdk`.
